The Password Manager System successfully met all its objectives. We tested the system with multiple users and observed the following:

User registration and login with OTP worked smoothly.

Passwords were securely stored and visible only to the logged-in user.

The password generator created random, strong passwords.

Saved credentials were shown correctly, and the copy feature functioned well.

The interface was easy to navigate, even for non-technical users.

Performance improved significantly after optimizing the code. Authentication time was reduced from 5–8 seconds to around 2 seconds. No storage errors occurred during testing, and user satisfaction was rated 9.4 out of 10 based on peer feedback.
